'@@author Rixte
@startuml
title Rejecting reset arguments and recovering at the next prompt
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false

actor User
participant MishMash
participant Parser
participant ResetPlanCommand as Reset
participant ActiveMealPlan as Active

User -> MishMash : reset-plan d/1
MishMash -> Parser : parseCommand("reset-plan d/1")
activate Parser
Parser -> Parser : parseResetPlan("d/1")
Parser --> MishMash : throws MishMashException
deactivate Parser
note over Parser, Active
  Rejection happens before a reset command is created.
  The plan, request, groceries, and other session data
  remain unchanged.
end note
MishMash --> User : error + Format: reset-plan + next prompt
User -> MishMash : reset-plan
MishMash -> Parser : parseCommand("reset-plan")
activate Parser
create Reset
Parser -> Reset : new ResetPlanCommand(activeMealPlan)
Parser --> MishMash : reset command
deactivate Parser
MishMash -> Reset : execute(recipeBook)
Reset -> Active : clear()
Active --> Reset
Reset --> MishMash : reset confirmation
MishMash --> User : result + next prompt
@enduml
'@@author
